=== PARITY (vs web components/layout/CopyLinkButton.tsx) ===
  Web source (58 lines): a ghost/sm <Button> that copies window.location.href to the
  clipboard (navigator.clipboard.writeText, with a legacy textarea+execCommand
  fallback), flips a transient `copied` state for 2000ms (Link2⇄Check icon, Copy
  link⇄Copied label), and fires toast.success / toast.error. Data sources:
  useTranslation + useToast. Charts/maps: none. Shared components: none.

  Data sources → bound through a push-based CopyLinkSource seam (P1/S8): the host
    surface pushes CopyLinkInput(shareURL, isLoading, errorMessage, connection,
    updatedAt). The web reads the LIVE url from window.location.href at click time;
    the native peer copies the latest pushed snapshot of the current view's shareable
    URL (the deep-link / route URL). The view performs NO networking and reaches for
    NO global — structurally enforced (view reads only the model; model reads only
    the source). teslasync:// is the app's deep-link scheme (Sources/App/AppRouteParser).
  Clipboard → CopyLinkClipboard seam; SystemCopyLinkClipboard wraps UIPasteboard
    (iOS/iPadOS) / NSPasteboard (macOS) — the native peer of navigator.clipboard.
    Returns Bool so the web try/catch success-vs-error branch is reproduced exactly.
  Toast → CopyLinkToast seam (success/error), the native peer of useToast; delegated
    to the host toast hub the same way diagnostics are. Success copy → success notice
    "Link copied to clipboard"; failed copy (or no URL) → error notice "Could not copy
    link" — verified executed-typecheck against both spy branches.
  Transient copied state → CopyLinkActionButton flips to Copied + checkmark for 2s
    (web setTimeout 2000), but ONLY on a successful copy (web sets copied inside the
    try), Reduce-Motion-aware, with a cancel-on-disappear Task.
  i18n → all 5 web keys reproduced verbatim (common.copyLink.action/copied/label/
    success/error); the view holds no English literals.

=== STATES (every one renders — no hidden surface) ===
  loading  → disabled chip + ProgressView + "Preparing link…"           (native leaf)
  empty    → muted chip "Nothing to share here" (no shareable URL)       (never blank)
  error    → "Link unavailable" + Retry (resolution failed)              (QueryError peer)
  ready    → the web Copy link ⇄ Copied button                          (web parity)
  stale    → ready + amber freshness chip + banner + 1-shot auto-refresh (live-state axis)
  offline  → ready (copies cached link) + muted chip + offline banner    (live-state axis)
  Branch priority (adapter): a usable URL always wins (so a stale/offline link is
  still copyable) → else error → else loading → else empty. Executed-typecheck-green.

